The inverted p-i-n stack places the HTL on the transparent substrate (so HTL/perovskite interface quality and hole selectivity dominate Voc and film morphology) and the ETL against the metal (so electron selectivity, hole blocking and contact chemistry dominate FF and stability). PTAA and doped NiO give the most favorable HOMO alignment with MAPbI3 together with low interfacial recombination; PMMA or Au nanoparticles further suppress recombination or raise Jsc. Fullerenes (PCBM or C60) plus BCP/Bphen (or PEI) furnish the required electron selectivity and metal diffusion barrier; Cu or Ag are chemically more benign than Al. Compact glass/ITO (or FTO) plus spin-coating produce the most uniform, low-defect absorber. These criteria immediately highlight five pool entries whose stacks are essentially identical to the highest-PCE training recipes:

- c038 adds PEI (dipole/extraction) and Au-np (conductivity + plasmonics) to the 20 % NiO device;
- c030 copies the 19.5 % PTAA/PMMA/Bphen device (PMMA passivation is decisive);
- c044 is the canonical high-performance PTAA/BCP/Cu stack;
- c097 is the direct analogue of the 18.5 % P3CT-Na/ITCPTC/C60-BCP cell;
- c041 uses the well-aligned, high-conductivity NiMgLiO HTL with a standard BCP/Ag contact.

Flexible substrates, PEDOT:PSS, missing hole-blockers, or Al contacts are all inferior on the same physical grounds and are therefore excluded.

Final: c038, c030, c044, c097, c041
